Z||000005||Joe Torma||08-02-2001||11:39 PM||||Hope you got everything fixed ok....That's what I don't want to happen!<BR>How high was too high?  Any higher than the photos above?<P>I'll probably drill a big enough hole and use hand-op metal nibblers for the top cut.<P>But I still need a dimension!!!  Help!<P>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000006||MooCow||08-03-2001||12:22 AM||||I drilled a whole first on my old SE.  Go 10" up and drill as far as you can to the left.  Cause the fuel pipe runs on the right top part of the whole.  You will have to make the subs more to one side than in the middle because of the fuel pipe.  Hope that helps.<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Joe Torma||08-03-2001||12:37 AM||||Thanks!<BR>10" hole from the bottom?  If so, then I will have plenty of room for the sub.  I didn't realize there was that much room in there!  The offset will be fine.<P>Joe<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||MooCow||08-03-2001||09:35 AM||||Now when I say as far over as you can to the left I am talking about still withint the cutout area.  If you look you should be able to see a box shape before you even cut into the firewall.  I believe the biggest it can get is 11" X 8".  I am not %100 on that but close to that.  I only cut out the drivers side and then stopped and ended up selling my SE.  I do plan on doing that thoe soon.<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000009||Joe Torma||08-03-2001||10:53 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MooCow:<BR><B>I believe the biggest it can get is 11" X 8<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's perfect.  My magnets are 8" in dia. Can anyone else confirm this?<BR>Thanks for the help so far.<P>Joe||||reg||1
